        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\{2,8,11\\}$",
          "worked": "Keep the elements of $B$ that are not in $A$:\n$$B\\cap\\overline A=\\{2,8,11\\}.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p58-q25-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$\\{x\\in A\\cup B\\text{ where }x\\text{ is odd}\\}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\{1,3,5,7,11\\}$",
          "worked": "The union is $\\{1,2,3,5,7,8,11\\}$. Keeping its odd elements gives $\\{1,3,5,7,11\\}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p58-q25-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$\\{X\\subseteq A\\text{ where }1\\in X\\text{ and }7\\notin X\\}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\big\\{\\{1\\},\\{1,3\\},\\{1,5\\},\\{1,3,5\\}\\big\\}$.\n\nInclude $1$, exclude $7$, and choose whether to include $3$ and $5$.",
          "worked": "Every subset must contain $1$ and omit $7$. The remaining elements $3$ and $5$ may each be included or omitted. The four choices give\n$$\\big\\{\\{1\\},\\{1,3\\},\\{1,5\\},\\{1,3,5\\}\\big\\}.$$",
